u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015MINUTES OF A REGULAR MEETING OF\rTHE CITY COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF CALABASAS,\rCALIFORNIA, HELD WEDNESDAY, JUNE 13, 2007\r\rMayor Bozajian called the meeting to order at 7:35 p.m. in the City Council Chambers of City Hall, 26135 Mureau Road, Calabasas, California.\r\rROLL CALL Present: Mayor Bozajian, Mayor pro Tem Maurer, Councilmembers Groveman, Wolfson.\r Absent: Councilmember Washburn.\r Staff: Bartlett, Bingham, Coroalles, Parker, Peirce, Permaul, Rubin, Tamuri.\r\rThe Pledge of Allegiance was led by Marth Scott Fritz.\r\rAPPROVAL OF AGENDA\r\r Councilmember Wolfson moved, seconded by Mayor pro Tem Maurer, to approve the agenda. MOTION CARRIED 4/0. Councilmember Washburn was absent. \r\rANNOUNCEMENTS/INTRODUCTIONS \r\rMayor Bozajian presented a plaque to Planning Commissioner Dave Brown in recognition of his being awarded the American Planning Association � LA 2007 Award for Distinguished Leadership�Citizen Planner. Mayor Bozajian presented plaques to Andrew Cohen-Cutler, former Environmental Commissioner and Cathey Sinai, former \u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015Public Safety Commissioner in recognition of their service to the City. Mayor Bozajian presented a proclamation to Deborah Low of the Las Virgenes Municipal Water District in honor of �Stop Runoff Month�. Councilmember Wolfson and Mayor pro Tem Maurer expressed their appreciation of staff and residents who assisted in the All-America City Award presentation. Mayor Bozajian announced the Mystery Movie Night will be taking place on June 29 at the Tennis & Swim Center. He spoke regarding the upcoming Council meeting schedule. He announced the 4th of July activities that will be occurring throughout the City and spoke regarding the upcoming Relay for Life event on June 23.\r\rORAL COMMUNICATIONS - PUBLIC COMMENT\r\r Spencer Armstrong, Calabasas, spoke regarding recent code enforcement actions on recreational vehicle parking in residential areas in the City.\r\rCONSENT ITEMS\r \r Approval of the minutes for the May 23, 2007 City Council meeting. \r \r Adoption of Resolution No. 2007-1082, accepting the sewer improvements for New Millennium Homes, Inc. Tract 35596 Phases 06-08, 09-Offsite, 09-15, 17-26 upon transfer of improvements to the Los Angeles County Sewer Maintenance District of the State of California. \r\r Recommendation to authorize staff to exonerate the Faithful Performance Bond specific to, sewer improvements only, for Tract 35596 Phases 06-08, 09-Offsite, 09-15, 17-26 and authorize staff to execute a replacement maintenance bond for one-year on all sewer improvements for the aforementioned tract and phases. \r\r Ratification of assignment of car-storage lease with Calabasas Motorcars in conjunction with sale of that company. \r\r Adoption of Resolution No. 2007-1087, approving the 16th cycle of Household Hazardous Waste Infrastructure Grant, Fiscal Year 2007-2008. \r\r Adoption of Resolution No 2007-1088, to approve a Proposed Joint Exercise of Powers Agreement between the County of Los Angeles and the City with respect to the County of Los Angeles Developer Fee Program for the benefit of the Consolidated Fire Protection District of Los Angeles County. \r\rCouncilmember Wolfson moved, seconded by Councilmember Groveman, to approve Consent Items # 1, 2, 3, 4, and 6. MOTION CARRIED 4/0. Councilmember Washburn was absent.\r\rFollowing discussion, Councilmember Wolfson moved, seconded by Councilmember Groveman, to approve Consent Item #5. MOTION CARRIED 3/1. Councilmember Washburn was absent and Mayor pro Tem Maurer voted no.\r\rUNFINISHED BUSINESS\r \r Discussion regarding workforce housing. \r\rTom Bartlett, City Planner, presented the staff report.\r\rThe City Council provided direction to staff to further develop a workforce housing program.\r\r Discussion regarding the City employee home buying assistance program.\r\rCity Manager Coroalles presented the staff report.\r\rLucy Martin, Calabasas, expressed concern over the proposed home buying assistance program. Dave Brown, Calabasas, spoke in support of the proposed home buying assistance program for City employees. Gail Schroeder, Calabasas, expressed concern over a bonus to employees. Martha Fritz, Calabasas, spoke regarding potential conflicts of interest that might arise with the proposed program. \r\rThe City Council provided direction to staff on an employee home buying assistance program.\r\rNEW BUSINESS\r \r Public meeting regarding the Landscape Maintenance District assessment proceedings.\r\rThere was no action taken.\r\r Discussion regarding the Draft Regional Housing Needs Assessment Allocation 2006-2014.\r\rThe item was continued to the meeting of July 11, 2007.\r \rINFORMATIONAL REPORTS\r\r Check Register for the period of May 15, 2007 to May 31, 2007. \r\rThere was no action taken.\r\rTASK FORCE REPORTS\r\r There were no task force reports.\r\rCITY MANAGER�S REPORT\r\r City Manager Coroalles indicated that he had nothing to report.\r\r\r\rFUTURE AGENDA ITEMS\r\r The following items were requested to be agendized for a future agenda:\r\rDiscussion regarding code enforcement of recreational vehicles in residential areas.\rDiscussion regarding expansion of the secondhand smoke ordinance.\r\rADJOURN\r\r The City Council adjourned at 9:20 p.m. in memory of Marlene Rubin and Carlos Lacamara.\r\r\r\r______________________________\rRobin Parker, City Clerk\r\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\r\r\r\r\r\u0013PAGE \u0014- 2 -\u0015\r\r\r\u0013PAGE \u0014- 3 -\u0015\r06/13/07\r\r\r\r\r\r\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0